{"task":"transcribe","language":"en","duration":138.176,"text":"Thanks for your help with that. I have gone through and done the regular hyperparameter tuning and everything, and your plan was very helpful. The next thing is, I wanted to work on doing patient-specific fine-tuning for the paper. And I wanted to get your input on what the right approach to doing it is. Essentially, the goal with patient-specific fine-tuning is take a small set of pulses from a particular patient, use them to further fine-tune the model, and then the idea is that in theory that makes your model better tuned to the patient, and you should see better results on that patient. So, I'm trying to figure out how to set this up. The full fine-tuned efficient net is what ends up performing the best out of all the tests I did. So, I want to use that for patient-specific fine-tuning. What do you think, how do you think I should structure this? I'm pretty sure that there's like one or two patients where I pretty much don't have any artifact data for. So, I can't use all of the patients. There's 10 patients in my test set, 10 patients in my validation set. And so I'm considering just using some of the test set patients to do this. I'm thinking about just picking five patients. And then for each of those five patients, they all have about somewhere around a total of 170 pulses each. I'm thinking of taking maybe 20 or 30 pulses and using those to do fine-tuning. But I'm not sure how many epochs I would do, what the batch size would be, what the learning rate is. This is a very, very, very small data set to be fine-tuning the model on. And so, I kind of just wanted to get your input on, like, do you think this would work with such a small data set? Do you think I should do some kind of augmentation? Is there a reliable way to do augmentation on this kind of data? What's your take?","segments":[{"id":0,"start":0.32,"end":1.76,"text":"Thanks for your help with that."},{"id":1,"start":2.0,"end":8.64,"text":"I have gone through and done the regular hyperparameter tuning and everything, and your plan was very helpful."},{"id":2,"start":9.28,"end":15.280000000000001,"text":"The next thing is, I wanted to work on doing patient-specific fine-tuning for the paper."},{"id":3,"start":23.6,"end":28.560000000000002,"text":"And I wanted to get your input on what the right approach to doing it is."},{"id":4,"start":28.88,"end":54.72,"text":"Essentially, the goal with patient-specific fine-tuning is take a small set of pulses from a particular patient, use them to further fine-tune the model, and then the idea is that in theory that makes your model better tuned to the patient, and you should see better results on that patient."},{"id":5,"start":55.52,"end":57.52,"text":"So, I'm trying to figure out how to set this up."},{"id":6,"start":58.480000000000004,"end":64.16,"text":"The full fine-tuned efficient net is what ends up performing the best out of all the tests I did."},{"id":7,"start":64.48,"end":67.6,"text":"So, I want to use that for patient-specific fine-tuning."},{"id":8,"start":67.92,"end":72.32000000000001,"text":"What do you think, how do you think I should structure this?"},{"id":9,"start":72.64,"end":80.08,"text":"I'm pretty sure that there's like one or two patients where I pretty much don't have any artifact data for."},{"id":10,"start":80.4,"end":82.48,"text":"So, I can't use all of the patients."},{"id":11,"start":82.72,"end":87.68,"text":"There's 10 patients in my test set, 10 patients in my validation set."},{"id":12,"start":88.56,"end":94.16,"text":"And so I'm considering just using some of the test set patients to do this."},{"id":13,"start":94.48,"end":98.0,"text":"I'm thinking about just picking five patients."},{"id":14,"start":98.88,"end":105.12,"text":"And then for each of those five patients, they all have about somewhere around a total of 170 pulses each."},{"id":15,"start":105.44,"end":112.32000000000001,"text":"I'm thinking of taking maybe 20 or 30 pulses and using those to do fine-tuning."},{"id":16,"start":112.64,"end":118.32000000000001,"text":"But I'm not sure how many epochs I would do, what the batch size would be, what the learning rate is."},{"id":17,"start":118.64,"end":123.28,"text":"This is a very, very, very small data set to be fine-tuning the model on."},{"id":18,"start":123.60000000000001,"end":130.72,"text":"And so, I kind of just wanted to get your input on, like, do you think this would work with such a small data set?"},{"id":19,"start":130.8,"end":133.12,"text":"Do you think I should do some kind of augmentation?"},{"id":20,"start":133.44,"end":136.8,"text":"Is there a reliable way to do augmentation on this kind of data?"},{"id":21,"start":137.20000000000002,"end":137.84,"text":"What's your take?"}]}